%description:

Tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary:off -- the end of a write that is not the end of the buffer has no PSH.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "false: the PSH of pushLastBufferedSegment".

The classes: off (false, the default), and two facets of on (true; LinuxTcp): write-end, PSH
on the segment that ends a write; long-write, PSH also inside a write longer than half the
largest window. The code: TcpConnection::sendSegment() and the marks of a SEND
(enqueueSendCommandData()). This test separates "off" from the facets of "on".

Host under test: host1, which writes 1448 bytes two times during its handshake, so both writes
wait in the buffer. Observation: level 1, the first data segment, the end of the first write,
has no PSH, and the second, the end of the buffer, has PSH.

%# parameter: Tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPushSegmentsOnWriteBoundaryOff")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 1448);
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 1448);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.pshBit == false")
             .describe("the first data segment, without PSH")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.pshBit == true")
             .describe("the second data segment, with PSH")
             .within(0.01));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPushSegmentsOnWriteBoundaryOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.pushSegmentsOnWriteBoundary = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPushSegmentsOnWriteBoundaryOff: PASS
